# Rimefall Milestone 1 — revision request

Your milestone 1 code works: automated tests confirm one tile per tick, pillar/wall blocking, no corner cutting, pause via Esc and Start, gamepad stick with deadzone, device switching, zero console errors. Now polish the visuals. Current files are below. Make ONLY these changes and output the COMPLETE contents of only the files you change (same === FILE === format). Do not change gameplay logic, the test hook window.__rimefall, or the module structure.

1. Snow particles: they currently render as hard opaque white squares, and flakes near the camera appear as huge squares. Make them small soft round flakes: generate a radial-gradient circular sprite texture with a CanvasTexture (no external files), transparent, depthWrite false, sizeAttenuation true, smaller size with slight variation, slight opacity (~0.8), gentle sway drift. Keep the particle volume around the play area and not between the camera and the player (no flakes closer than ~4 units to the camera).
2. Floor contrast: the floor is washed out (almost white, flat). Give it a cooler icy look: tiles in pale blue-grey with a bit more per-tile variation (some tiles slightly bluer "ice", some whiter "packed snow"), grid lines a little more visible but still subtle. Slightly reduce hemisphere light intensity / adjust tone so pillars and the player have readable shading and visible shadows on the floor. Keep fog light blue.
3. Player: scale the player placeholder up ~25% so it reads clearly at this camera distance; give the head a skin tone and a simple helmet/hood with contrast against the blue tunic; keep it chunky low-poly.
4. True-tile marker (OSRS style): draw a thin glowing outline (square line loop, slightly above the floor, yellow-ish, ~60% opacity) on the player's CURRENT logical tile (snaps each tick, not interpolated), since the mesh glides between tiles. Create it in render.js (not an entity).
5. Camera: pull the camera back slightly (~10%) and lower the FOV a bit so the near room edge is less cut off; keep smooth follow.

